    solution: "<h2>User</h2><p>Working adults aged 22 to 40 who are learning a new language on their phones, usually for travel or a job.</p><h2>Job to be done</h2><p>When I have a few minutes on the bus, I want to practise speaking without feeling silly, so I can feel I am making real progress.</p><h2>Pain</h2><p>They lose motivation after a few days, because lessons feel repetitive and they cannot tell whether they are improving.</p><h2>Evidence</h2><p>Analytics show that 58% of new users do not return after day 7, and 9 of 12 interviewees said they stopped because they could not see progress.</p><h2>Opportunity</h2><p>If we show clear weekly progress and a short speaking challenge, we could raise week-two retention by 15%, from 42% to about 48%.</p>",
