    solution: "<h1>HostelBite</h1><h2>Users and problem</h2><p>Students living in hostels near our college cannot get affordable, hygienic food after 9 pm, and they spend about 30 minutes finding options. About 4000 students live within two kilometres of campus.</p><h2>Vision</h2><p>Become the easiest way for hostel students to get a trusted, fairly priced meal at any hour.</p><h2>North Star metric</h2><p>Weekly meals ordered per active student, with a target of 2.5 within six months.</p><h2>Priorities</h2><ol><li>Reliable delivery within 30 minutes, because late delivery is the top reason users leave.</li><li>A simple weekly meal plan with fixed low prices, because students budget by the week.</li><li>Partner with five hygiene-rated kitchens, because trust in quality decides repeat orders.</li></ol><h2>Roadmap</h2><p>Now: launch ordering and tracking for two hostels.</p><p>Next: weekly meal plans and a loyalty offer.</p><p>Later: late-night snack partnerships and group orders.</p><h2>Risks</h2><ul><li>Food safety incidents. Response: only work with licensed kitchens and inspect them monthly.</li><li>Low delivery capacity at peak times. Response: limit orders per slot and add riders gradually.</li></ul>",
